From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 18:30:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] domicile: a site's "Sign in with" dialogs ask the shell

FedCM ("Sign in with Google"'s account chooser) was off, since Chrome
draws its dialogs over the outermost window, which for a <webview> is
the shell's (#1985). Its dialogs now ask the page's element instead.

- `chrome_content_browser_client.cc`:
  CreateIdentityRequestDialogController returns
  `domicile::MakeIdentityDialog`
  (`chrome/browser/domicile/domicile_identity_dialog.h`), which asks
  the guest's element for each step and opens the provider's own pages
  as browser windows.
- Blink build lists: DomicileIdentityEvent and its two dictionaries.

Verified: not built. This repository cannot build Chromium; the engine
job builds it on `crux`.
---
 chrome/browser/chrome_content_browser_client.cc           | 5 ++++-
 third_party/blink/renderer/bindings/generated_in_core.gni | 6 ++++++
 third_party/blink/renderer/bindings/idl_in_core.gni       | 3 +++
 third_party/blink/renderer/core/html/build.gni            | 2 ++
 4 files changed, 15 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/chrome/browser/chrome_content_browser_client.cc b/chrome/browser/chrome_content_browser_client.cc
index 3fbbe3d..1ddec54 100644
--- a/chrome/browser/chrome_content_browser_client.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/chrome_content_browser_client.cc
@@ -4,6 +4,7 @@
 
 #include "chrome/browser/chrome_content_browser_client.h"
 
+#include "chrome/browser/domicile/domicile_identity_dialog.h"
 #include "components/domicile/browser/force_dark.h"
 #include "components/domicile/browser/shell_source.h"
 #include "components/domicile/browser/shell_url_loader_factory.h"
@@ -8959,7 +8960,9 @@ bool ChromeContentBrowserClient::HasErrorPage(int http_status_code) {
 std::unique_ptr<content::IdentityRequestDialogController>
 ChromeContentBrowserClient::CreateIdentityRequestDialogController(
     content::WebContents* web_contents) {
-  return std::make_unique<IdentityDialogController>(web_contents);
+  // Domicile's engine fork: the shell shows a site's "Sign in with" dialogs,
+  // not Chrome. See chrome/browser/domicile/domicile_identity_dialog.h.
+  return domicile::MakeIdentityDialog(web_contents);
 }
 
 std::unique_ptr<content::DigitalIdentityProvider>
